Ladybird puts an inside ::marker ahead of its list item’s first block
child, in an anonymous block of its own. The other engines all do the
same. Gecko’s nsCSSFrameConstructor::ProcessChildren() constructs the
marker before the list item’s other children, and nsBlockFrame::
AddFrames() starts a new line for the block child after it. Blink’s
LayoutBlockFlow::AddChild() keeps the inline marker in insertion order
while it wraps inline content around block children. And WebKit’s
RenderTreeBuilder::List::buildInlineMarker() attaches the marker ahead
of the list item’s first child whenever parentForInlineMarker() finds
that child to be an authored block, rather than an anonymous one.
